schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-vegalite-03-teaching-exploration-widget
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: kino-vegalite
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: teaching-exploration-widget
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook educator. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.VegaLite. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Teach declarative chart structure through runnable examples and concise comments.
  text: |-
    Create a Kino.VegaLite teaching and exploration cell that demonstrates how a Vega-Lite spec is built in Elixir. Use deterministic local data and show at least three chart variations, such as bar, line, scatter with brush selection, and heatmap. Include comments explaining Vl.new, data_from_values, mark, encode_field, explicit type values, transform, param, layering or concat, and when Kino.Plotly is better for 3D or scientific figures.

    Requirements: include Livebook compatibility, Chart smart cell compatibility notes, a companion Kino.DataTable or data preview, fallback local data, accessible labels and color schemes, and safe execution checks. Avoid remote URLs unless they are clearly optional. Do not stream into a bare VegaLite spec.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-vegalite-teaching-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino_vega_lite, vega_lite, kino, and optionally uses Kino.DataTable for preview."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino and Chart smart cell relevance."
  - "Reactive state: selection params and any streaming examples use correct VegaLite or Kino.VegaLite state boundaries."
  - "Data shape: local rows, preview data, field names, explicit field types, and transforms are documented."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: labels, legends, tooltips, color schemes, data preview, and fallback data are present."
  - "Safe execution: no required remote URLs, credentials, eval, shell commands, giant inline data, or push calls on a bare spec."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "The code is valid and every encode_field call includes explicit type."
    - "Multiple chart examples render through VegaLite or Kino.VegaLite correctly."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Teaches VegaLite DSL structure, encodings, transforms, params, and composition."
    - "Includes data preview or table pairing to support notebook exploration."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Examples are small, clear, and arranged for learning."
    - "Charts use readable labels, legends, tooltips, and accessible color schemes."
    - "The data preview helps learners connect rows to encodings."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles missing values, empty rows, temporal sorting, duplicate categories, and unsupported chart choices."
    - "Uses deterministic local data."
    - "Documents when to choose Plotly, MapLibre, or DataTable instead."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.VegaLite-centered and teaches declarative charting accurately."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-vegalite
- teaching-exploration-widget

